; `file:..` from this app points at its own parent directory. npm would link it,
; and a package symlinked to a path outside the project root breaks Metro: a
; module this package loads lazily resolves its relative imports against the app
; root and never loads, so the app refuses with "this build cannot show a
; desktop surface". Installing the dependency packed puts it inside this app's
; node_modules, where Metro resolves it the same way it resolves every other
; dependency. After editing the package, reinstall here to pick the change up.
install-links=true
